B.EN=new A.cf("Syndromes","Infantile spasms","With developmental regression, a pediatric neurologic emergency requiring urgent EEG (hypsarrhythmia) and treatment.",B.cs)
B.ER=new A.cf("Syndromes","Catamenial pattern","Best confirmed with a seizure diary correlated against a menstrual calendar, not by history alone.",B.dX)
B.EU=new A.cf("Syndromes","Reflex epilepsy triggers","Photosensitive, reading, musicogenic, hot water and startle epilepsies share a stereotyped trigger-to-seizure relationship \u2014 ask specifically.",B.bP)
B.F1=new A.cf("Mimics","Convulsive syncope","The single most commonly misdiagnosed seizure mimic in adults \u2014 look for a presyncopal prodrome and rapid full recovery.",B.cs)
B.EP=new A.cf("Mimics","Anoxic myoclonus","Brief myoclonic jerks during a faint do not make an event epileptic.",B.bP)
B.ES=new A.cf("Mimics","Bedside glucose","Always check during the acute evaluation of any transient event \u2014 hypoglycemia is a readily reversible mimic.",B.dX)
B.EX=new A.cf("Mimics","Migraine aura tempo","Migraine with aura evolves more slowly (minutes) than an epileptic aura (seconds) and is usually followed by headache.",B.bP)
B.F3=new A.cf("Investigations","Normal EEG \u2260 no epilepsy","A single normal interictal EEG does not exclude epilepsy \u2014 sensitivity rises with sleep-deprived and repeated recordings.",B.dX)
B.EV=new A.cf("Investigations","Video-EEG monitoring","Capturing a typical habitual event remains the diagnostic gold standard when the differential is unclear.",B.dX)
B.EM=new A.cf("Investigations","CK & lactate rise","Elevated CK and a transient venous lactate rise support a recent convulsive epileptic seizure.",B.bP)
